  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q49-55-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q49-55-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{\\cos(90^\\circ-(-\\theta))}\\\\\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{\\sin(-\\theta)}\\\\\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=-\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=-\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q49-55-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sec\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{\\sin(90^\\circ+\\theta)}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{\\sin(90^\\circ-(-\\theta))}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{\\cos(-\\theta)}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\sec\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q49-55-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cot(90^\\circ+\\theta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\tan\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cot(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{\\cos(90^\\circ+\\theta)}{\\sin(90^\\circ+\\theta)}\\\\\\cot(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=\\frac{-\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\cot(90^\\circ+\\theta)&=-\\tan\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q49-55-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sec(90^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cot\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sec(90^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta}{\\sec\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\sec(90^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\sec(90^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\cot\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nRetain the original restrictions $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q49-55-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\operatorname{cosec}(270^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan\\theta$\n\nUse periodicity and complementary identities, then simplify the reciprocal quotient.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(270^\\circ-\\theta)&=\\sin(-90^\\circ-\\theta)\\\\\\sin(270^\\circ-\\theta)&=-\\sin(90^\\circ+\\theta)\\\\\\sin(270^\\circ-\\theta)&=-\\cos\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}(270^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\frac{-\\sec\\theta}{-\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}(270^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}(270^\\circ-\\theta)}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\tan\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nRetain the original restrictions $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q49-55-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sin(270^\\circ-\\theta)\\cos(90^\\circ+\\theta)}{\\tan(90^\\circ-\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sin^2\\theta$\n\nTransform the three shifted functions before cancelling factors.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin(270^\\circ-\\theta)\\cos(90^\\circ+\\theta)}{\\tan(90^\\circ-\\theta)}&=\\frac{(-\\cos\\theta)(-\\sin\\theta)}{\\cot\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\sin(270^\\circ-\\theta)\\cos(90^\\circ+\\theta)}{\\tan(90^\\circ-\\theta)}&=\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\sin(270^\\circ-\\theta)\\cos(90^\\circ+\\theta)}{\\tan(90^\\circ-\\theta)}&=\\sin^2\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nRetain the original restrictions $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q49-55-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}+\\dfrac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\cos(90^\\circ+\\theta)+\\sin(90^\\circ+\\theta)\\\\\\frac{1}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=-\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta\\\\\\frac{1}{\\sec(90^\\circ+\\theta)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosec}(90^\\circ+\\theta)}&=\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nRetain the original restrictions $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
